    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Launch LIONESS-DRAGON on rna_all.csv (60 samples by 2,000 genes) and prot_all.csv (the same 60 samples by 500 proteins). Estimate the lambdas automatically, write the all-sample matrix to agg_dragon.tsv and the per-sample table to per_sample_edges.tsv, and start it right away."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"Launch LIONESS-DRAGON on rna_all.csv (60 samples by 2,000 genes) and prot_all.csv (the same 60 samples by 500 proteins).\" -- not available here as asked. NetZoo's LIONESS-DRAGON has no setting for \"Estimate the lambdas automatically\"; the settings it passes are lambda1 and lambda2. LIONESS-DRAGON writes at most 20,000,000 values (features x (features - 1) / 2 x samples); 2,500 features and 60 samples give 187,425,000.\n2. \"write the all-sample matrix to agg_dragon.tsv\" -- not available here as asked. NetZoo's LIONESS-DRAGON has no setting for \"write the all-sample matrix to agg_dragon.tsv\"; the settings it passes are lambda1 and lambda2.\n3. \"the per-sample table to per_sample_edges.tsv\" -- not available here as asked. NetZoo's LIONESS-DRAGON has no setting for \"the per-sample table to per_sample_edges.tsv\"; the settings it passes are lambda1 and lambda2.\n4. \"start it right away\" -- not available here as asked. NetZoo's LIONESS-DRAGON has no setting for \"start it right away\"; the settings it passes are lambda1 and lambda2.\n\nNo registered workflow can give these as you asked them (above), so none is offered as asked.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
